00:17:33,480 --> 00:17:35,040
There's no power to run it.

286
00:17:35,400 --> 00:17:36,120
Could be manual.

287
00:17:36,400 --> 00:17:36,520
Huh?

288
00:17:37,200 --> 00:17:38,260
Sounds boring.

289
00:17:39,420 --> 00:17:40,440
What are those?

290
00:17:40,720 --> 00:17:41,440
Shogi puzzles?

291
00:17:42,280 --> 00:17:42,980
Old school.

292
00:17:43,500 --> 00:17:44,420
I think it's interesting.

293
00:17:45,120 --> 00:17:45,420
Huh?

294
00:17:45,420 --> 00:17:45,560
Huh?

295
00:17:45,560 --> 00:17:52,060
Come with one.

296
00:17:52,060 --> 00:17:53,740
It's an amazingims Twice

297
00:17:53,740 --> 00:17:54,720
on house.

298
00:17:54,900 --> 00:17:56,140
What about you?

299
00:17:56,140 --> 00:17:58,600
Huh?

300
00:17:58,600 --> 00:17:59,080
What about you?

301
00:17:59,080 --> 00:17:59,840
That's so nice.

302
00:17:59,900 --> 00:18:00,540
This is my life.

303
00:18:00,600 --> 00:18:02,640
I think it's a hard time for you, you know.

304
00:18:02,780 --> 00:18:03,440
What about you?

305
00:18:03,440 --> 00:18:05,320
Love you too.

306
00:18:05,460 --> 00:18:06,360
What about you?

307
00:18:06,360 --> 00:18:06,380
Time for you.

308
00:18:06,380 --> 00:18:07,460
Good to you.

309
00:18:07,460 --> 00:18:08,340
Hi, learning.

310
00:18:08,340 --> 00:18:08,460
What?

311
00:18:08,460 --> 00:18:08,720
Do we love you.

312
00:18:08,720 --> 00:18:09,920
What about you?

313
00:18:09,920 --> 00:18:10,100
I think it's beautiful.

314
00:18:10,100 --> 00:18:10,300
You're a ghost witch?

315
00:18:10,300 --> 00:18:10,920
I think it's a dream entre family,

316
00:18:10,920 --> 00:18:11,080
right?

317
00:18:11,080 --> 00:18:11,480
What about you?

318
00:18:11,480 --> 00:18:12,160
You're a nightmare.

319
00:18:12,160 --> 00:18:12,580
What about you?

320
00:18:12,580 --> 00:18:42,560
I don't know.

321
00:18:42,580 --> 00:19:12,560
I don't know.

322
00:19:12,580 --> 00:19:42,560
I don't know.

323
00:19:42,560 --> 00:19:45,280
Oh, um, my name's Kokoro.

324
00:19:46,080 --> 00:19:47,580
Yeah, I remember.

325
00:19:48,560 --> 00:19:49,420
Headed back already?

326
00:19:52,480 --> 00:19:53,080
Bye!

327
00:19:53,080 --> 00:19:55,700
Hey, Kokoro!

328
00:19:56,360 --> 00:19:58,080
You guys, Kokoro's here!

329
00:19:59,080 --> 00:20:00,400
We waited for you.

330
00:20:00,800 --> 00:20:02,180
Glad you made it back, Kokoro.

331
00:20:02,800 --> 00:20:03,740
Long time.

332
00:20:04,120 --> 00:20:04,320
Yo.

333
00:20:05,120 --> 00:20:08,260
I, uh, I haven't had any time to visit.

334
00:20:08,960 --> 00:20:09,500
Oh, okay.

335
00:20:10,320 --> 00:20:12,840
We've all been coming quite a bit since that first time.

336
00:20:13,380 --> 00:20:15,820
We mostly get together around this time in the afternoon.

337
00:20:16,620 --> 00:20:19,300
Though I probably show up a little later in the day than all of you.

338
00:20:19,820 --> 00:20:21,120
You're pretty early today.

339
00:20:21,640 --> 00:20:22,440
I have practice.

340
00:20:22,880 --> 00:20:23,220
Soccer.

341
00:20:23,800 --> 00:20:24,520
But not today.

342
00:20:25,520 --> 00:20:26,360
Someone else is coming.

343
00:20:26,360 --> 00:20:26,800
Hmm?

344
00:20:26,800 --> 00:20:27,040
Hmm?

345
00:20:29,540 --> 00:20:29,980
Ah!

346
00:20:30,780 --> 00:20:32,040
Good to see everyone!

347
00:20:33,040 --> 00:20:33,780
Kokoro's here!

348
00:20:36,340 --> 00:20:38,060
Now it's all seven of us.

349
00:20:39,100 --> 00:20:40,960
I'll be in my room if you need me.

350
00:20:41,360 --> 00:20:41,640
Wait!

351
00:20:41,880 --> 00:20:42,180
Aki!

352
00:20:42,620 --> 00:20:43,580
Where are you going?

353
00:20:44,580 --> 00:20:45,980
I only just got here.

354
00:20:45,980 --> 00:20:50,900
By the way, I brought some of my mom's special cookies for you to try.

355
00:20:51,140 --> 00:20:52,120
They're really good.

356
00:20:52,500 --> 00:20:53,220
Take a hint.

357
00:20:53,800 --> 00:20:54,480
I can't watch.

358
00:20:56,000 --> 00:20:58,580
I guess I missed out on things while I was gone.

359
00:20:59,340 --> 00:21:01,040
But they were happy to see me.

360
00:21:02,600 --> 00:21:03,820
I'll go again tomorrow.

361
00:21:15,980 --> 00:21:21,940
Hey, Kokoro!

362
00:21:22,780 --> 00:21:22,980
Huh?

363
00:21:23,360 --> 00:21:24,360
Come, over here!

364
00:21:28,220 --> 00:21:29,280
Boys are in there.

365
00:21:29,540 --> 00:21:30,940
They're too annoying to deal with.

366
00:21:31,320 --> 00:21:33,420
Though it's more Urashino than the other three.

367
00:21:33,620 --> 00:21:34,600
Come down with us!

368
00:21:34,600 --> 00:21:48,580
We spend a lot of our time in here.

369
00:21:49,500 --> 00:21:51,040
And you can't beat that view.

370
00:21:53,040 --> 00:21:53,480
Huh.

371
00:21:53,480 --> 00:22:04,800
Check it out.

372
00:22:05,100 --> 00:22:06,980
I found these beautiful teacups here.

373
00:22:07,340 --> 00:22:09,120
But no running water to make tea.

374
00:22:09,420 --> 00:22:10,500
Or a working stove.

375
00:22:11,120 --> 00:22:13,020
So you have to bring your own drinks.

376
00:22:14,200 --> 00:22:15,360
Here, have some.

377
00:22:15,900 --> 00:22:16,860
Thank you very much.

378
00:22:19,860 --> 00:22:20,340
Delicious.

379
00:22:21,040 --> 00:22:22,340
Is this strawberry tea?

380
00:22:22,700 --> 00:22:23,300
That's right.

381
00:22:23,800 --> 00:22:24,880
I'm glad you like it.

382
00:22:25,300 --> 00:22:26,020
I sure do.

383
00:22:28,580 --> 00:22:31,260
Um, have you looked around the castle a little?

384
00:22:31,620 --> 00:22:33,120
You don't have to be so nervous.

385
00:22:33,800 --> 00:22:35,460
We have, but just a little bit.

386
00:22:36,900 --> 00:22:40,200
The day after we first arrived, Fuka and I did some exploring.

387
00:22:43,240 --> 00:22:45,080
We even went all the way up to the tower.

388
00:22:45,080 --> 00:22:58,640
The castle is completely surrounded by water, with no land in sight.

389
00:22:58,640 --> 00:23:03,740
You also spent some time looking for the key, but no luck.

390
00:23:03,740 --> 00:23:10,420
I was wondering if they find the key, then...

391
00:23:10,420 --> 00:23:14,900
Oh, how are your rooms?

392
00:23:14,900 --> 00:23:16,080
Mine's really nice.

393
00:23:16,520 --> 00:23:18,540
Yeah, mine is really cool too.

394
00:23:19,120 --> 00:23:21,120
Fuka even has a piano in hers.

395
00:23:21,120 --> 00:23:24,880
I wanted to ask them what their wishes were.

396
00:23:27,440 --> 00:23:28,500
But I couldn't.

397
00:23:30,680 --> 00:23:34,720
To be honest, I wouldn't want them to ask me either.

398
00:23:34,720 --> 00:23:46,340
Coming to the castle is a lot of fun.

399
00:23:46,340 --> 00:23:50,680
Whether I'm hanging out with the others, or by myself.

400
00:23:50,680 --> 00:23:54,200
All of them come here almost every day.

401
00:23:55,240 --> 00:23:57,220
I wonder if they're skipping school just like me.

402
00:23:58,220 --> 00:24:01,200
But no one asks, or even admits to it.

403
00:24:02,240 --> 00:24:04,880
In a way, it's kind of comforting.

404
00:24:11,640 --> 00:24:13,480
Well, they're pretty tasty, don't you think?

405
00:24:14,000 --> 00:24:15,060
Here, take a few more.

406
00:24:15,260 --> 00:24:16,360
You don't have to be shy about it.

407
00:24:18,160 --> 00:24:18,960
Hey, Kokoro!

408
00:24:20,680 --> 00:24:26,920
Why don't you come over here with me?

409
00:24:27,060 --> 00:24:27,580
Right this way.

410
00:24:32,520 --> 00:24:33,540
Don't just stand there.

411
00:24:33,700 --> 00:24:34,580
Have a seat next to me.

412
00:24:34,920 --> 00:24:36,200
These are some of my mom's cookies.

413
00:24:36,640 --> 00:24:38,260
Please go and have as many as you'd like.

414
00:24:38,660 --> 00:24:40,420
I saved the prettiest ones just for you.

415
00:24:42,240 --> 00:24:42,640
Thanks.

416
00:24:43,380 --> 00:24:45,900
You think that move works on the other girls you stratted on?

417
00:24:47,960 --> 00:24:49,680
So, I wanted to ask you.

418
00:24:49,680 --> 00:24:52,540
Do you have a boyfriend or someone you like like that?

419
00:24:52,540 --> 00:24:56,840
Hey, you.

420
00:24:57,840 --> 00:25:01,100
So what?

421
00:25:01,320 --> 00:25:04,020
You decided to switch your focus from Aki to Kokoro now?

422
00:25:04,520 --> 00:25:06,980
Wolf Queen, it's been a while since we last saw you.

423
00:25:07,640 --> 00:25:08,420
Well, come on.

424
00:25:08,960 --> 00:25:10,000
Why are you lazing about?

425
00:25:10,780 --> 00:25:12,160
Shouldn't you be looking for the key?

426
00:25:12,840 --> 00:25:14,140
I don't think it's here.

427
00:25:14,140 --> 00:25:16,280
Maybe you're not looking hard enough.

428
00:25:17,480 --> 00:25:20,080
Well, I guess it doesn't matter if none of you have any wishes.

429
00:25:22,540 --> 00:25:23,620
Urashina's got a wish.

430
00:25:23,740 --> 00:25:24,460
That's for sure.

431
00:25:24,740 --> 00:25:26,360
Kokoro, look deep into my eyes.

432
00:25:26,520 --> 00:25:27,220
Oh, please.

433
00:25:28,500 --> 00:25:30,480
You didn't hear any of that, right?

434
00:25:32,020 --> 00:25:32,980
It's so stupid.

435
00:25:32,980 --> 00:25:42,120
It's so stupid.

436
00:25:42,300 --> 00:25:43,200
Drop dead.

437
00:25:43,200 --> 00:26:01,680
I went home for a bit to have some lunch, but now I'm back.

438
00:26:01,680 --> 00:26:05,000
So, uh, oh, the others are playing games upstairs.

439
00:26:07,900 --> 00:26:11,920
Hey, since we're great friends and all, Fuca, do you happen to have a nickname you go by?

440
00:26:12,200 --> 00:26:14,180
Maybe Fufu or something like that.

441
00:26:14,440 --> 00:26:14,940
I don't.

442
00:26:15,440 --> 00:26:17,360
My mom just called me clean old Fuca.

443
00:26:17,840 --> 00:26:19,600
Yeah, guess I can see that.

444
00:26:20,020 --> 00:26:21,280
Oh, oh, one more question.

445
00:26:21,280 --> 00:26:27,660
I can't.

446
00:26:27,840 --> 00:26:28,460
Too hard.

447
00:26:28,660 --> 00:26:29,360
I need a break.

448
00:26:39,920 --> 00:26:40,720
Nobody's here.

449
00:26:41,260 --> 00:26:42,140
That's a first.

450
00:26:42,140 --> 00:26:52,140
What's this?

451
00:26:53,240 --> 00:26:53,600
Kokoro.

452
00:26:54,100 --> 00:26:54,320
Ah!

453
00:26:54,880 --> 00:26:56,400
Sorry, didn't mean to scare you.

454
00:26:57,320 --> 00:26:57,700
Mm-hmm.

455
00:26:58,280 --> 00:26:59,900
I didn't know anyone was here.

456
00:27:00,840 --> 00:27:03,780
I'm pretty sure that everyone else is busy over summer break.

457
00:27:04,540 --> 00:27:05,340
Oh, really?

458
00:27:05,840 --> 00:27:07,200
Masamune is with his parents.

459
00:27:08,200 --> 00:27:11,460
Fuca said that she has two weeks of seminar this time during the afternoons.

460
00:27:12,140 --> 00:27:14,280
And Urashino goes to cram school somewhere.

461
00:27:15,480 --> 00:27:15,720
Oh.

462
00:27:19,720 --> 00:27:21,560
Oh, Fuf.

463
00:27:24,020 --> 00:27:24,340
Yo!

464
00:27:28,340 --> 00:27:29,100
Going home?

465
00:27:29,560 --> 00:27:30,740
Uh-huh.

466
00:27:31,820 --> 00:27:34,240
It seems like the others haven't been coming much.

467
00:27:35,680 --> 00:27:37,260
Maybe it's because of summer break?

468
00:27:37,520 --> 00:27:37,880
Uh-huh.

469
00:27:38,580 --> 00:27:41,160
I think they all have summer seminars or something.

470
00:27:42,140 --> 00:27:43,340
Seminars, huh?

471
00:27:43,700 --> 00:27:44,520
What's that?

472
00:27:45,100 --> 00:27:45,280
Eh?

473
00:27:45,920 --> 00:27:49,700
It's like a class where they review what they taught you during first term.

474
00:27:51,020 --> 00:27:51,700
Wow.

475
00:27:52,540 --> 00:27:54,140
Everyone is so studious.

476
00:27:55,240 --> 00:27:56,540
Are you going to?

477
00:27:57,200 --> 00:27:57,420
Huh?

478
00:27:58,480 --> 00:27:59,140
I don't know.

479
00:27:59,840 --> 00:28:00,860
That's a relief.

480
00:28:00,860 --> 00:28:05,820
This is nice.

481
00:28:06,620 --> 00:28:07,720
I feel better now.

482
00:28:12,000 --> 00:28:12,440
Huh?

483
00:28:12,740 --> 00:28:13,520
Don't worry.

484
00:28:13,720 --> 00:28:14,460
I'm not upset.

485
00:28:15,020 --> 00:28:17,960
I think it's great that you're finally going out and getting some fresh air.

486
00:28:18,640 --> 00:28:22,080
I was just surprised to find that you weren't at home when I stopped by.

487
00:28:23,080 --> 00:28:24,480
Why did you come back home?

488
00:28:24,820 --> 00:28:25,620
To spy on me?

489
00:28:26,420 --> 00:28:26,860
No.

490
00:28:27,180 --> 00:28:27,980
Of course not.

491
00:28:28,380 --> 00:28:31,580
My plans changed last minute and I thought we could have lunch together.

492
00:28:32,140 --> 00:28:33,760
I don't want you to monitor me.

493
00:28:36,680 --> 00:28:37,720
Mrs. Kitajima.

494
00:28:37,720 --> 00:28:44,520
You know, the teacher you spoke to at the alternative school, she was asking about you.

495
00:28:45,960 --> 00:28:47,060
She reached out.

496
00:28:47,540 --> 00:28:49,920
She was hoping that the two of you could talk together again.

497
00:28:50,640 --> 00:28:54,680
She knows you can't go back to school, but she knows it's not your fault.

498
00:28:55,060 --> 00:28:57,180
There has to be some reason behind this.

499
00:28:57,480 --> 00:28:59,020
It's what she keeps telling me.

500
00:28:59,520 --> 00:29:00,720
That's why...

501
00:29:00,720 --> 00:29:02,320
Oh, that's your dad.

502
00:29:02,660 --> 00:29:03,540
He's home early.

503
00:29:03,540 --> 00:29:06,820
Hey, why don't we all sit down together?

504
00:29:17,640 --> 00:29:18,740
Summer break, right?

505
00:29:19,340 --> 00:29:20,820
Yeah, but...

506
00:29:20,820 --> 00:29:22,580
Summer break is pretty much over.

507
00:29:23,480 --> 00:29:24,720
Yeah, good point.

508
00:29:24,720 --> 00:29:27,820
Aren't you afraid the teachers will get mad at you?

509
00:29:28,920 --> 00:29:32,360
Everybody's gonna be on edge if you walk into school with your hair dyed like that.

510
00:29:32,680 --> 00:29:35,100
Well, yeah, but I don't really care.

511
00:29:35,560 --> 00:29:35,920
Hmm.

512
00:29:38,820 --> 00:29:40,400
I think it looks good on you.

513
00:29:41,040 --> 00:29:42,680
Maybe I'll try something like that.

514
00:29:43,520 --> 00:29:45,920
Hey, maybe all three of us should try it.

515
00:29:46,140 --> 00:29:46,360
Huh?

516
00:29:47,220 --> 00:29:47,420
Oh.

517
00:29:47,420 --> 00:29:54,380
Although, if I make Fuca do something silly like that, somebody here might get upset.

518
00:29:55,420 --> 00:29:58,320
You already gave Fuca a gift earlier, am I right?

519
00:29:58,720 --> 00:30:00,480
Mommy's special homemade cookies.

520
00:30:07,380 --> 00:30:08,560
Listen up!

521
00:30:09,700 --> 00:30:13,300
Next term, I've decided that I'm gonna go back to school.

522
00:30:13,300 --> 00:30:17,160
I was being polite before, so I didn't say anything till now.

523
00:30:17,480 --> 00:30:20,620
But everyone who comes here, none of you go to school, right?

524
00:30:21,400 --> 00:30:23,260
You can't go to school, am I right?

525
00:30:25,400 --> 00:30:26,600
It's so stupid!

526
00:30:27,220 --> 00:30:30,000
Even you, Aki, you were acting all worried.

527
00:30:30,280 --> 00:30:31,600
What would the teachers think, huh?

528
00:30:32,220 --> 00:30:33,280
What a joke.

529
00:30:34,380 --> 00:30:35,640
Don't talk like that.

530
00:30:35,940 --> 00:30:36,540
Why not?

531
00:30:36,880 --> 00:30:38,540
All of you guys treated me like a joke.

532
00:30:38,980 --> 00:30:39,880
You always do.

533
00:30:40,240 --> 00:30:42,080
You laugh at me, right in my face.

534
00:30:42,080 --> 00:30:43,700
No, that's not true.

535
00:30:45,020 --> 00:30:47,300
Although, maybe it is true.

536
00:30:48,080 --> 00:30:50,340
Like, it was okay to make fun of Urashino.

537
00:30:51,540 --> 00:30:53,180
I'm sick and tired of it!

538
00:30:53,820 --> 00:30:55,100
All of us are the same!

539
00:30:55,460 --> 00:30:56,160
We're losers!

540
00:30:56,600 --> 00:30:57,080
Outsiders!

541
00:30:57,520 --> 00:30:58,980
None of us have any friends!

542
00:30:59,240 --> 00:31:00,180
You're all the same!

543
00:31:00,500 --> 00:31:01,320
And you as well!

544
00:31:01,800 --> 00:31:02,780
You're the same too!

545
00:31:03,000 --> 00:31:03,780
And you, Fuca!

546
00:31:04,100 --> 00:31:04,760
Kokuro, you!

547
00:31:05,060 --> 00:31:06,220
All of you are the same!

548
00:31:06,820 --> 00:31:08,720
Urashino, you need to calm down.

549
00:31:08,720 --> 00:31:12,320
Why don't you tell us what's going on with you first?

550
00:31:12,560 --> 00:31:14,240
What's the reason you stopped going to school?

551
00:31:14,620 --> 00:31:15,280
Go ahead!

552
00:31:15,760 --> 00:31:16,980
What did I...

553
00:31:16,980 --> 00:31:18,120
I didn't.

554
00:31:18,420 --> 00:31:19,360
I still go to school.

555
00:31:22,040 --> 00:31:22,560
Liar!

556
00:31:22,720 --> 00:31:23,580
I'm not lying.

557
00:31:24,420 --> 00:31:26,720
Although, the school isn't in Japan.

558
00:31:27,160 --> 00:31:29,180
I actually go to a boarding school in Hawaii.

559
00:31:29,880 --> 00:31:30,400
Hawaii?

560
00:31:30,820 --> 00:31:32,320
Like, Hawaii, Hawaii?

561
00:31:33,200 --> 00:31:35,700
Uh, that's pretty far away, isn't it?

562
00:31:36,340 --> 00:31:36,780
Yeah.

563
00:31:37,320 --> 00:31:38,260
But that doesn't matter.

564
00:31:39,360 --> 00:31:39,900
Wait a second.

565
00:31:40,360 --> 00:31:42,400
The Wolf Queen said something the first day.

566
00:31:42,840 --> 00:31:47,600
She said the castle's hours were 9 o'clock in the morning till 5 o'clock at night Japan time.

567
00:31:48,120 --> 00:31:50,240
I was wondering why she mentioned the time zone.

568
00:31:51,240 --> 00:31:52,740
Are you, like, rich or something?

569
00:31:53,100 --> 00:31:53,300
Huh?

570
00:31:54,180 --> 00:31:56,200
No, it's actually nothing like that at all.

571
00:31:56,820 --> 00:32:01,620
The school itself was pretty easy to get into, and we mostly focused on training and playing soccer.

572
00:32:01,620 --> 00:32:04,100
Here, you're studying abroad for soccer.

573
00:32:04,440 --> 00:32:04,660
Really?

574
00:32:05,120 --> 00:32:05,360
Hmm.

575
00:32:05,780 --> 00:32:06,040
Yeah.

576
00:32:06,300 --> 00:32:07,600
Why didn't you tell any of us?

577
00:32:07,940 --> 00:32:09,080
You think you're better than us?

578
00:32:09,540 --> 00:32:10,840
Is that what it really is?

579
00:32:11,340 --> 00:32:14,420
Uh, uh, no, of course I don't think that.

580
00:32:15,240 --> 00:32:19,320
At first, I thought everyone else here was studying abroad the same as I was.

581
00:32:20,040 --> 00:32:22,940
But then everybody started talking about afternoons in Japan.

582
00:32:23,540 --> 00:32:26,400
I honestly couldn't tell if you were going to school or not.

583
00:32:27,240 --> 00:32:29,360
I came later because of the time zone.

584
00:32:29,360 --> 00:32:30,720
I don't care.

585
00:32:31,120 --> 00:32:32,060
None of it matters.

586
00:32:32,740 --> 00:32:34,520
I'm going to do what the rest of you couldn't.

587
00:32:34,940 --> 00:32:36,680
I'm going to show you all that I'm different.

588
00:32:37,240 --> 00:32:38,840
I'm going back to school next term.

589
00:32:39,340 --> 00:32:40,160
I'm leaving.

590
00:32:40,160 --> 00:33:10,140
I'm leaving.

591
00:33:10,140 --> 00:33:11,900
It isn't as bad as it looks, though.

592
00:33:16,900 --> 00:33:18,740
Urashino, want to play?

593
00:33:19,520 --> 00:33:20,540
How about it?

594
00:33:21,080 --> 00:33:21,940
Play with us.

595
00:33:22,560 --> 00:33:22,880
Okay?

596
00:33:23,180 --> 00:33:23,620
Come on.

597
00:33:23,620 --> 00:33:34,920
I can't believe that happened to him, but it is Urashino.

598
00:33:34,920 --> 00:33:37,640
I guess I can't be too surprised about it.

599
00:33:37,760 --> 00:33:38,440
You know what I mean?

600
00:33:38,920 --> 00:33:43,320
He said after he started middle school, his new friends got him to pay for things constantly,

601
00:33:43,600 --> 00:33:46,080
and it looks like things just continue to escalate from there.

602
00:33:46,080 --> 00:33:51,620
I know what it sounds like, but they weren't bullying me or anything like that.

603
00:33:51,840 --> 00:33:53,480
I hadn't seen them all in a while.

604
00:33:53,960 --> 00:33:56,560
Things were kind of awkward, so I thought I should apologize to them.

605
00:33:57,260 --> 00:33:58,060
And I did.

606
00:33:58,060 --> 00:34:01,380
It sounds like they should be the ones apologizing.

607
00:34:02,640 --> 00:34:06,180
According to the teacher, they were all worried about me the whole time I was out.

608
00:34:06,660 --> 00:34:10,020
But when we talked, all they said is that I'm useless if I didn't pay for things.

609
00:34:10,860 --> 00:34:14,180
That's when I snapped and shoved one of them, and they shoved back.

610
00:34:14,180 --> 00:34:15,660
Oh, boy.

611
00:34:16,700 --> 00:34:19,880
I guess this is a safe space for all of us, even Urashino.

612
00:34:20,540 --> 00:34:22,360
I wanted to ask...

613
00:34:22,360 --> 00:34:22,560
Hmm?

614
00:34:24,160 --> 00:34:25,040
Um...

615
00:34:25,040 --> 00:34:27,140
Well, I...

616
00:34:27,140 --> 00:34:29,500
I noticed you haven't come to the castle in a while.

617
00:34:29,820 --> 00:34:30,360
Why's that?

618
00:34:31,100 --> 00:34:31,580
Hmm.

619
00:34:32,000 --> 00:34:32,720
That's true.

620
00:34:33,100 --> 00:34:33,380
What?

621
00:34:37,100 --> 00:34:38,780
I have a boyfriend now.

622
00:34:39,120 --> 00:34:39,440
Huh?

623
00:34:40,460 --> 00:34:41,580
Keep it a secret.

624
00:34:44,180 --> 00:35:11,960
It's been a while.

625
00:35:12,320 --> 00:35:13,140
Are you doing well?

626
00:35:13,800 --> 00:35:14,200
Yeah.

627
00:35:18,280 --> 00:35:18,860
Come in.

628
00:35:19,360 --> 00:35:21,280
I can't stay long, so we can talk right here.

629
00:35:21,840 --> 00:35:25,240
I thought about waiting for your mother so that the three of us could speak together.

630
00:35:25,660 --> 00:35:28,700
But I figured it'd be best if just the two of us talked first.

631
00:35:29,980 --> 00:35:32,280
And your mother and I talk every now and then.

632
00:35:33,060 --> 00:35:37,160
It would be nice to have you start coming to our school at some point, once you're feeling up to it.

633
00:35:37,160 --> 00:35:47,180
You said something to my mother about it not being my fault.

634
00:35:47,180 --> 00:35:51,360
Did you really say that?

635
00:35:51,360 --> 00:35:53,360
It surprised me.

636
00:35:53,900 --> 00:35:54,100
Hmm.

637
00:35:54,100 --> 00:35:56,720
W-why?

638
00:35:56,720 --> 00:35:56,780
Why?

639
00:36:00,780 --> 00:36:01,800
I said it.

640
00:36:02,180 --> 00:36:04,220
Because you're fighting every single day.

641
00:36:04,320 --> 00:36:04,940
Isn't that true?

642
00:36:04,940 --> 00:36:16,380
Can I visit again sometime?

643
00:36:16,880 --> 00:36:17,360
Sure.

644
00:36:17,360 --> 00:36:23,540
This is some of the tea I like to drink.

645
00:36:23,820 --> 00:36:25,380
I thought that you might like to have some.

646
00:36:25,780 --> 00:36:26,920
I hope that you'll take it.

647
00:36:28,280 --> 00:36:28,720
Yes.

648
00:36:28,900 --> 00:36:29,880
Thank you very much.

649
00:36:29,880 --> 00:36:31,360
I'll see you later.

650
00:36:51,360 --> 00:36:55,700
Since all seven of us happened to be here today, I think it's time to talk things over.

651
00:36:56,120 --> 00:36:56,980
What should we do from here?

652
00:36:56,980 --> 00:37:00,520
It's October, so we've only got six months left.

653
00:37:01,280 --> 00:37:03,100
And we still haven't found the key yet.

654
00:37:03,580 --> 00:37:05,240
We've looked pretty thoroughly.

655
00:37:05,820 --> 00:37:07,580
Masamune and I both searched together.

656
00:37:09,620 --> 00:37:12,580
I spent a day searching by myself.

657
00:37:13,720 --> 00:37:15,760
Masamune snuck up on me in the dining room.

658
00:37:16,340 --> 00:37:17,680
You were focused on your search.

659
00:37:17,980 --> 00:37:19,440
That's why you didn't hear me come in.

660
00:37:20,040 --> 00:37:21,520
You waited till we all left.

661
00:37:21,720 --> 00:37:24,800
So that way you could search for the key all by yourself every day.

662
00:37:24,800 --> 00:37:27,840
Except I couldn't find it.

663
00:37:28,300 --> 00:37:30,460
So I think we should work together to look for it.

664
00:37:31,180 --> 00:37:32,180
We may be rivals.

665
00:37:32,720 --> 00:37:38,980
But if we find it, I figure we could just decide whose wish gets granted by drawing straws or rock, paper, scissors or something.

666
00:37:39,500 --> 00:37:41,160
I'm a little surprised to hear this, Aki.

667
00:37:41,320 --> 00:37:42,860
I didn't even know you had a wish.

668
00:37:42,860 --> 00:37:45,800
Or that you were so keen on this, Masamune.

669
00:37:47,460 --> 00:37:50,360
I mean, doesn't everyone have a wish or two that's important to them?

670
00:37:51,240 --> 00:37:51,780
I'm in.

671
00:37:52,160 --> 00:37:52,660
Me too.

672
00:37:53,340 --> 00:37:56,740
But if we're gonna do this, how about we promise one thing?

673
00:37:57,800 --> 00:38:01,880
Even if one of us finds the key, let's not use it until late March.

674
00:38:02,400 --> 00:38:03,360
Good idea!

675
00:38:03,700 --> 00:38:05,420
It would suck to lose this place.

676
00:38:05,420 --> 00:38:06,340
Yeah.

677
00:38:07,000 --> 00:38:08,060
What do you think?

678
00:38:08,680 --> 00:38:08,940
Huh.

679
00:38:10,660 --> 00:38:13,080
Okay then, let's figure out who goes where.

680
00:38:17,620 --> 00:38:18,100
Nope.

681
00:38:18,560 --> 00:38:21,200
Aki did tell us that she searched the kitchen pretty thoroughly.

682
00:38:21,460 --> 00:38:23,880
Even so, we might be able to find something she missed.

683
00:38:26,920 --> 00:38:27,400
Huh?

684
00:38:27,540 --> 00:38:28,280
What's this?

685
00:38:29,060 --> 00:38:31,400
Oh, I was wondering what that cross was for.

686
00:38:31,720 --> 00:38:32,700
I noticed it earlier.

687
00:38:32,700 --> 00:38:36,280
Are you okay?

688
00:38:36,540 --> 00:38:37,920
Your arm hasn't healed yet?

689
00:38:39,140 --> 00:38:40,900
Yeah, but it's feeling a lot better.

690
00:38:41,360 --> 00:38:42,580
Except when I stretch it.

691
00:38:43,660 --> 00:38:44,000
Huh.

692
00:38:45,160 --> 00:38:46,480
Hey, Fuuka.

693
00:38:47,340 --> 00:38:50,860
Before, I said a lot of weird stuff because I was angry.

694
00:38:51,620 --> 00:38:53,060
But I really like it here.

695
00:38:55,120 --> 00:38:56,580
Staying at the castle was fun.

696
00:38:57,480 --> 00:38:57,680
Hmm.

697
00:38:59,440 --> 00:38:59,700
Huh.

698
00:38:59,700 --> 00:39:03,320
So you won't be going back to school then?

699
00:39:04,200 --> 00:39:05,220
No, I won't.

700
00:39:06,280 --> 00:39:09,240
But the other school I go to has a really great teacher.

701
00:39:09,780 --> 00:39:11,000
The alternative school?

702
00:39:12,440 --> 00:39:16,000
The teacher there is always checking in on me and asking me what I want.

703
00:39:16,740 --> 00:39:18,980
When I talk, she really listens.

704
00:39:20,860 --> 00:39:21,220
Wow.

705
00:39:21,220 --> 00:39:21,280
Wow.

706
00:39:21,280 --> 00:39:21,340
Wow.

707
00:39:21,340 --> 00:39:21,380
Wow.

708
00:39:21,380 --> 00:39:23,340
Wow.

709
00:39:23,340 --> 00:39:23,660
Wow.

710
00:39:23,660 --> 00:39:23,680
Wow.

711
00:39:23,680 --> 00:39:23,720
Wow.

712
00:39:29,700 --> 00:39:30,200
Wow.

713
00:39:32,680 --> 00:39:33,840
Oh, crap.

714
00:39:34,780 --> 00:39:35,520
Hey!

715
00:39:36,280 --> 00:39:37,920
Time's up, guys!

716
00:39:38,860 --> 00:39:40,280
No luck, huh?

717
00:39:41,320 --> 00:39:43,420
Well, there's nothing else we can do today.

718
00:39:43,900 --> 00:39:45,460
Let's find time to search again.

719
00:39:50,760 --> 00:39:52,740
What marvelous solidarity.

720
00:39:52,740 --> 00:39:59,520
Hi there. We meet again, Little Red Riding Hoods.

721
00:39:59,700 --> 00:40:00,900
Out of nowhere, as usual.

722
00:40:02,040 --> 00:40:04,320
You all seem to be having a lot of fun together.

723
00:40:05,240 --> 00:40:06,700
I had to see it for myself.

724
00:40:07,120 --> 00:40:08,520
I hope this won't be a problem.

725
00:40:09,300 --> 00:40:11,220
We can search for the key together, right?

726
00:40:12,000 --> 00:40:12,920
Yes, cooperate.

727
00:40:14,340 --> 00:40:15,520
It's lovely to see.

728
00:40:16,680 --> 00:40:17,660
One more thing.

729
00:40:18,280 --> 00:40:19,860
I forgot to mention it before.

730
00:40:19,860 --> 00:40:20,220
Huh?

731
00:40:20,220 --> 00:40:23,860
When you find the key, and a wish has been granted,

732
00:40:24,680 --> 00:40:27,320
all your memories of this place will vanish.

733
00:40:27,860 --> 00:40:28,860
What do you mean?

734
00:40:29,360 --> 00:40:33,020
This castle, and all your time spent here, will be forgotten.

735
00:40:33,960 --> 00:40:37,480
You won't remember each other, me, or anything else.

736
00:40:39,520 --> 00:40:43,740
On the other hand, if no one's wishes granted by March 30th,

737
00:40:44,160 --> 00:40:45,280
you'll keep your memories.

738
00:40:45,280 --> 00:40:49,240
And you'll all continue to remember the time you spent here.

739
00:40:50,220 --> 00:40:52,100
The choice is up to you.

740
00:40:53,680 --> 00:40:54,940
Whatever you decide.

741
00:40:58,360 --> 00:41:02,340
To be honest, speaking for myself, I'm fine if I lose these memories.

742
00:41:03,100 --> 00:41:04,240
I'm fine with that.

743
00:41:07,780 --> 00:41:09,900
Because we wouldn't have met otherwise.

744
00:41:10,580 --> 00:41:11,320
You know what I mean?

745
00:41:11,320 --> 00:41:15,000
Aki, does your wish really mean that much to you?

746
00:41:23,000 --> 00:41:23,500
I, uh...

747
00:41:24,300 --> 00:41:24,560
Hmm?

748
00:41:24,560 --> 00:41:30,440
So, uh, there's this girl, Sanada, who has been a big problem for me.

749
00:41:34,020 --> 00:41:39,440
Right when school started, this pretty transfer student named Moe Tojo joined her class.

750
00:41:39,440 --> 00:41:48,420
She lived across the street from me, and we became friends pretty quickly.

751
00:41:52,640 --> 00:41:54,060
Sanada's really popular.

752
00:41:54,680 --> 00:41:55,560
She's not shy.

753
00:41:56,160 --> 00:41:58,580
She's always surrounded by people who want to be her friend.

754
00:41:58,580 --> 00:42:02,900
Even the teachers couldn't help liking her.

755
00:42:05,040 --> 00:42:08,460
What is it?

756
00:42:08,860 --> 00:42:10,900
You know, I hate ugly girls.

757
00:42:11,260 --> 00:42:12,040
Girls like you.

758
00:42:13,040 --> 00:42:15,560
Are you happy now?

759
00:42:15,560 --> 00:42:23,380
Did you really think that Ikeda would ask you out?

760
00:42:23,860 --> 00:42:25,480
Well, I guess you thought wrong.

761
00:42:25,760 --> 00:42:29,080
Seriously, Ikeda would never actually fall for a girl like you.

762
00:42:29,340 --> 00:42:30,340
It's so stupid.

763
00:42:30,580 --> 00:42:31,440
Drop dead.

764
00:42:31,980 --> 00:42:36,540
That boy Ikeda, back in elementary school, he told me once that he had a crush on me.

765
00:42:36,540 --> 00:42:39,520
But, it was just the once.

766
00:42:41,800 --> 00:42:45,640
Then, when we started junior high, Sanada started dating Ikeda.

767
00:42:47,340 --> 00:42:49,140
That wasn't even the worst of it.

768
00:43:00,420 --> 00:43:01,820
Kokoro, are you there?

769
00:43:06,540 --> 00:43:14,400
There wasn't just a couple of people outside my house.

770
00:43:14,800 --> 00:43:15,980
It felt like a whole group.

771
00:43:16,500 --> 00:43:17,280
Come on out!

772
00:43:17,520 --> 00:43:18,660
Yeah, make it quick!

773
00:43:18,960 --> 00:43:19,800
Don't hide!

774
00:43:20,020 --> 00:43:21,100
I know you're in there.

775
00:43:21,260 --> 00:43:22,280
Let's try the backyard.

776
00:43:22,540 --> 00:43:23,460
We can check the window.

777
00:43:23,760 --> 00:43:25,680
You better come out or we'll crash your garden.

778
00:43:26,800 --> 00:43:28,660
What have you been doing in this?

779
00:43:28,720 --> 00:43:30,060
She's too rare to come out.

780
00:43:30,080 --> 00:43:31,600
Kokoro, have a way with us!

781
00:43:31,620 --> 00:43:32,940
You better come out wherever you are.

782
00:43:32,940 --> 00:43:34,660
You shouldn't be eyeing someone else's boyfriend.

783
00:43:34,680 --> 00:43:36,180
Sanada, that has something to say to you.

784
00:43:36,180 --> 00:43:37,460
Don't be such a baby.

785
00:43:38,220 --> 00:43:39,140
It looked open.

786
00:43:39,300 --> 00:43:40,800
She's totally in there.

787
00:43:41,160 --> 00:43:43,660
Get out here, you stupid coward!

788
00:43:44,540 --> 00:43:45,480
Get out here.

789
00:43:46,260 --> 00:43:48,860
Come on, show yourself!

790
00:43:49,380 --> 00:43:51,400
Mom, mom, mom!

791
00:43:52,180 --> 00:43:54,180
That girl, how could she...

792
00:43:55,920 --> 00:43:58,000
Sanada, please don't cry.

793
00:43:58,500 --> 00:44:00,600
Stupid girl came on to her boyfriend.

794
00:44:00,600 --> 00:44:02,420
She deserves what's coming.

795
00:44:03,040 --> 00:44:04,380
I hate you!

796
00:44:04,460 --> 00:44:05,240
Stop hiding!

797
00:44:05,240 --> 00:44:06,160
Open up!

798
00:44:06,200 --> 00:44:07,640
Why aren't you coming out?

799
00:44:07,760 --> 00:44:09,000
I won't forgive you!

800
00:44:09,460 --> 00:44:10,800
Take me all you want.

801
00:44:11,080 --> 00:44:12,020
Don't forgive me.

802
00:44:12,280 --> 00:44:14,340
Because I will never forgive you either.

803
00:44:16,340 --> 00:44:17,500
I panicked.

804
00:44:17,500 --> 00:44:21,680
To be honest, I thought they were really going to kill me.

805
00:44:21,680 --> 00:44:24,700
Before I knew it, the whole house was dark.

806
00:44:25,180 --> 00:44:26,800
And it was all quiet outside.

807
00:44:28,200 --> 00:44:31,000
It wasn't long until my mom came back home.

808
00:44:31,860 --> 00:44:34,100
But I couldn't tell her what happened.

809
00:44:34,820 --> 00:44:35,720
I don't know why.

810
00:44:35,720 --> 00:44:42,640
And because of all that, I eventually stopped going to school.

811
00:44:42,640 --> 00:44:53,600
You're safe.

812
00:44:53,600 --> 00:44:54,600
Okay?

813
00:44:55,160 --> 00:44:56,920
You've been brave for so long.

814
00:44:57,440 --> 00:44:57,600
Hmm.

815
00:44:58,420 --> 00:44:58,980
Well done.

816
00:44:58,980 --> 00:45:05,280
I wanted to tell somebody.

817
00:45:07,080 --> 00:45:09,580
I wanted somebody to listen to me.

818
00:45:09,580 --> 00:45:19,620
I thought if it wasn't for Sanada, everything would be easier.

819
00:45:19,620 --> 00:45:26,460
I wanted to find the key and wish for her to disappear from this world, so we'd never have to see her again.

820
00:45:27,420 --> 00:45:28,420
But I...

821
00:45:28,420 --> 00:45:31,360
I don't want to lose my memories of all of you.

822
00:45:31,360 --> 00:45:35,360
I have no idea what I'm supposed to do.

823
00:45:48,420 --> 00:45:51,900
Despite everything that happened, we continue to look for the key.

824
00:45:54,420 --> 00:45:55,820
Have you tried to work this?

825
00:45:57,200 --> 00:45:58,260
Oh, that.

826
00:45:59,140 --> 00:46:01,260
None of us have been able to figure out what it is.

827
00:46:02,080 --> 00:46:03,560
I think I might know.

828
00:46:03,900 --> 00:46:04,040
Huh?

829
00:46:15,400 --> 00:46:16,000
Then.

830
00:46:16,580 --> 00:46:16,780
Hmm?

831
00:46:16,780 --> 00:46:32,640
Is this a music box?

832
00:46:32,880 --> 00:46:33,080
Hmm.

833
00:46:33,080 --> 00:46:47,780
Hey, what's going on in here?

834
00:46:51,940 --> 00:46:53,000
How's it doing that?

835
00:46:53,000 --> 00:46:55,160
Rion figured out how it works.

836
00:46:55,940 --> 00:46:56,960
It's toy, Morai.

837
00:46:57,440 --> 00:46:57,900
Oh.

838
00:46:58,960 --> 00:47:01,420
This must be an antique music box.

839
00:47:02,080 --> 00:47:02,720
It's lovely.

840
00:47:04,520 --> 00:47:06,260
What's wrong?

841
00:47:10,340 --> 00:47:15,600
Are you okay?

842
00:47:16,640 --> 00:47:17,520
What's wrong?

843
00:47:18,000 --> 00:47:19,340
She showed up like this.

844
00:47:19,980 --> 00:47:20,340
Aki?

845
00:47:23,000 --> 00:47:24,240
Sorry.

846
00:47:24,640 --> 00:47:25,640
I'm fine, you guys.

847
00:47:34,440 --> 00:47:36,160
Uh, what?

848
00:47:38,000 --> 00:47:39,380
That school uniform.

849
00:47:40,660 --> 00:47:42,020
It's Yuki Shina's.

850
00:47:45,080 --> 00:47:45,760
Hmm.

851
00:47:46,300 --> 00:47:47,420
So you figured it out.

852
00:47:47,860 --> 00:47:49,180
Yeah, it's surprising.

853
00:47:50,000 --> 00:47:53,960
All seven of us go to the same junior high school, Yuki Shina and Minami, Tokyo.

854
00:47:54,320 --> 00:47:54,640
Mm-hmm.

855
00:47:55,400 --> 00:47:55,760
Right.

856
00:47:56,240 --> 00:47:58,880
I got sent to boarding school before entering junior high.

857
00:47:59,880 --> 00:48:02,660
If I stayed, that's the school I would have gone to.

858
00:48:02,820 --> 00:48:04,040
There are a lot of us here.

859
00:48:04,040 --> 00:48:06,820
And we're all not going to our junior high school.

860
00:48:07,580 --> 00:48:07,940
Huh.

861
00:48:10,100 --> 00:48:15,500
Maybe if you talked to each other more, you little red riding hoods would have figured this out a lot sooner.

862
00:48:15,500 --> 00:48:18,260
Oh, well.

863
00:48:19,260 --> 00:48:21,120
You seem to be enjoying all of this.

864
00:48:22,060 --> 00:48:22,620
Oh, no.

865
00:48:22,980 --> 00:48:25,600
I am not one to have such wicked motives in my heart.

866
00:48:26,040 --> 00:48:27,200
Then explain all this.

867
00:48:27,760 --> 00:48:30,020
Just what is it you want from us?

868
00:48:30,560 --> 00:48:31,460
Nothing to speak of.

869
00:48:31,460 --> 00:48:33,580
I don't want anything from you.

870
00:48:34,420 --> 00:48:38,620
This place and the chance to find the key is all that I offer to you, Seven.

871
00:48:39,140 --> 00:48:40,920
Nothing more and nothing less.

872
00:48:43,100 --> 00:48:44,280
They're all here.

873
00:48:44,840 --> 00:48:46,360
We're together in the same town.

874
00:48:48,120 --> 00:48:50,540
It makes me feel better for some reason.

875
00:48:52,740 --> 00:48:53,920
Oh, my gosh.

876
00:48:55,240 --> 00:48:57,760
Up till now, I couldn't tell you.

877
00:48:57,760 --> 00:49:03,320
I wanted to, but I just couldn't.

878
00:49:06,780 --> 00:49:09,560
I had no idea at all.

879
00:49:11,420 --> 00:49:12,240
Look, Mom.

880
00:49:12,600 --> 00:49:14,400
This wasn't just some argument we had.

881
00:49:14,920 --> 00:49:16,280
It was so much worse.

882
00:49:22,360 --> 00:49:24,360
Then we'll fight, okay?

883
00:49:25,400 --> 00:49:27,260
You and I will fight this together.

884
00:49:28,320 --> 00:49:28,640
Kokoro.

885
00:49:30,280 --> 00:49:31,160
I'm sorry.

886
00:49:31,820 --> 00:49:32,780
I'm so sorry.

887
00:49:33,000 --> 00:49:33,820
I should have noticed.

888
00:49:41,420 --> 00:49:42,040
Thank you.

889
00:49:44,920 --> 00:49:46,540
Kokoro, it's been a while.

890
00:49:47,220 --> 00:49:47,620
You well?

891
00:49:49,340 --> 00:49:51,780
Well, I'm happy we can finally speak.

892
00:49:52,280 --> 00:49:53,520
I've been asking about you.

893
00:49:54,380 --> 00:49:55,260
Mrs. Kitajima.

894
00:49:55,700 --> 00:49:57,260
Wasn't she supposed to be here as well?

895
00:49:58,220 --> 00:49:59,800
This is simply a school issue.

896
00:49:59,920 --> 00:50:00,840
I don't see the need.

897
00:50:01,380 --> 00:50:02,680
I've already spoken with Sanada.

898
00:50:03,200 --> 00:50:04,800
I'm happy to clear up any misunderstanding.

899
00:50:06,120 --> 00:50:06,560
Misunderstanding?

900
00:50:07,100 --> 00:50:07,740
How's this?

901
00:50:08,820 --> 00:50:12,080
We could set up a meeting between you and Miss Sanada to talk things out.

902
00:50:13,160 --> 00:50:14,500
Hey, look up here.

903
00:50:15,320 --> 00:50:16,660
Hey, Mr. Hark.

904
00:50:16,660 --> 00:50:20,120
We're up here.

905
00:50:23,120 --> 00:50:25,460
You know, Mr. Ida's such a dumbass.

906
00:50:25,680 --> 00:50:26,220
For real.

907
00:50:26,220 --> 00:50:30,840
You know, she's the kind of girl that's easy to misunderstand.

908
00:50:30,840 --> 00:50:34,220
And I know you've been having a tough time yourself, Kokoro.

909
00:50:34,940 --> 00:50:36,960
However, Sanada said she's sorry.

910
00:50:37,500 --> 00:50:38,480
And she's worried about her.

911
00:50:38,480 --> 00:50:39,860
I seriously doubt she's sorry.

912
00:50:40,580 --> 00:50:45,440
And if she really is worried, it's only because a teacher scolded her for what she had done.

913
00:50:45,820 --> 00:50:49,200
What she's scared of is a teacher thinking badly of her.

914
00:50:49,440 --> 00:50:50,420
And nothing else.

915
00:50:50,420 --> 00:50:53,960
Kokoro, I'm not so sure that we've...

916
00:50:53,960 --> 00:50:58,220
Mr. Ida, shouldn't you start by asking Kokoro what happened and getting her side of the story?

917
00:50:59,520 --> 00:51:03,700
If that other girl was able to do so, shouldn't you be doing the same for my daughter?

918
00:51:03,740 --> 00:51:04,440
Yes, of course.

919
00:51:04,720 --> 00:51:07,860
Although, I do believe the two of them should be able to work...

920
00:51:07,860 --> 00:51:08,340
That's quite enough.

921
00:51:08,800 --> 00:51:13,420
The next time you come, I should like the first year's administrator or the principal to accompany you as well.

922
00:51:13,560 --> 00:51:14,460
Is that understood?

923
00:51:14,460 --> 00:51:17,940
Whoa.

924
00:51:20,480 --> 00:51:21,560
That's beautiful.

925
00:51:22,500 --> 00:51:23,660
Homemade? From a girl?

926
00:51:24,560 --> 00:51:26,760
Uh, kinda. My mom.

927
00:51:27,300 --> 00:51:28,300
She makes one every year.

928
00:51:29,360 --> 00:51:30,340
She visits for Christmas.

929
00:51:31,060 --> 00:51:32,040
She's flying back now.

930
00:51:33,000 --> 00:51:34,500
Already? That's quick.

931
00:51:34,700 --> 00:51:35,680
Two nights, three days.

932
00:51:36,080 --> 00:51:36,880
She's pretty busy.

933
00:51:37,460 --> 00:51:38,220
Oh, I see.

934
00:51:38,800 --> 00:51:40,420
Alright, let's dig in already!

935
00:51:40,940 --> 00:51:42,160
Yeah, let's eat!

936
00:51:42,160 --> 00:51:44,540
Hey, why don't we invite the Wolf Queen?

937
00:51:45,640 --> 00:51:46,620
Good idea.

938
00:51:46,960 --> 00:51:47,400
You called?

939
00:51:48,980 --> 00:51:49,980
Every time.

940
00:51:50,500 --> 00:51:51,260
Christmas cake.

941
00:51:51,640 --> 00:51:53,300
My mom makes it every year.

942
00:51:53,580 --> 00:51:55,900
We've got the Christmas version of the Wolf Queen today.

943
00:51:56,320 --> 00:51:56,980
Sure do.

944
00:51:57,560 --> 00:51:58,500
It's really cute.

945
00:52:01,860 --> 00:52:04,120
Hang on. Can you eat with your mask on?

946
00:52:05,180 --> 00:52:07,060
No. I can't eat here.

947
00:52:08,140 --> 00:52:10,660
You can cut me a piece. I'll eat by myself.

948
00:52:10,660 --> 00:52:13,640
I never thought you'd say yes.

949
00:52:14,000 --> 00:52:16,160
Who would have guessed that the Wolf Queen likes cake too?

950
00:52:22,040 --> 00:52:24,560
Hey, I've got something I need to ask you guys.

951
00:52:24,560 --> 00:52:34,100
Do you think you could all come to school for the third term for me?

952
00:52:34,560 --> 00:52:36,360
Even if it is, just for a day or two.

953
00:52:39,040 --> 00:52:42,480
My folks, they want me to transfer to a different junior high.

954
00:52:43,640 --> 00:52:46,400
Even though I thought going to the other school was enough for them.

955
00:52:46,660 --> 00:52:48,900
You go there? To the alternative school? Really?

956
00:52:48,900 --> 00:52:51,340
Yeah. I mean, sometimes.

957
00:52:51,680 --> 00:52:53,020
They've got this one cool teacher there.

958
00:52:53,240 --> 00:52:54,420
Hold on. Which teacher?

959
00:52:54,720 --> 00:52:55,140
A woman?

960
00:52:55,760 --> 00:52:57,620
And is her name Mrs. Kitajima, by chance?

961
00:52:58,060 --> 00:52:58,580
Yeah.

962
00:52:59,960 --> 00:53:00,980
Wow. Really?

963
00:53:01,520 --> 00:53:04,500
Problem is, it isn't exactly a real school.

964
00:53:05,240 --> 00:53:06,800
We don't study all that much.

965
00:53:07,480 --> 00:53:08,560
So private school, then.

966
00:53:09,240 --> 00:53:11,760
Your folks have no faith in public school teachers, right?

967
00:53:11,760 --> 00:53:12,500
Yeah.

968
00:53:13,140 --> 00:53:15,040
My dad is really well connected.

969
00:53:15,700 --> 00:53:17,960
He's gonna set something up for me, so.

970
00:53:18,520 --> 00:53:20,300
My parents and I have talked about it, too.

971
00:53:21,200 --> 00:53:23,500
That somewhere else might work out better, right?

972
00:53:26,140 --> 00:53:26,900
I'm worried.

973
00:53:27,400 --> 00:53:31,000
If I transfer, what if I can't come back to the castle?

974
00:53:31,320 --> 00:53:31,540
Huh?

975
00:53:32,260 --> 00:53:34,000
So I talked to my dad.

976
00:53:34,640 --> 00:53:37,900
I told him I want to go back to Yukishina, at least for the third term.

977
00:53:38,280 --> 00:53:40,100
But you'll just...

978
00:53:40,100 --> 00:53:41,720
Just come for the first day.

979
00:53:42,380 --> 00:53:44,180
That's all I'm asking you to do.

980
00:53:45,480 --> 00:53:45,960
Please.

981
00:53:47,160 --> 00:53:49,080
You don't even have to go to class.

982
00:53:49,640 --> 00:53:51,280
We can meet in the nurse's office.

983
00:53:51,700 --> 00:53:53,120
Or the library.

984
00:53:54,360 --> 00:53:58,000
Maybe it's not a coincidence we all go to the same school.

985
00:54:00,240 --> 00:54:02,280
Maybe we're supposed to look out for each other.

986
00:54:11,760 --> 00:54:15,180
It's okay.

987
00:54:15,180 --> 00:54:17,040
You didn't have to take the day off from work.

988
00:54:17,660 --> 00:54:18,460
Are you sure?

989
00:54:18,680 --> 00:54:19,560
I can go with you.

990
00:54:20,360 --> 00:54:20,660
Mm-mm.

991
00:54:21,220 --> 00:54:22,120
I'll be all right.

992
00:54:22,680 --> 00:54:24,020
Well, I better go.

993
00:54:24,960 --> 00:54:26,060
Please take care.

994
00:54:26,060 --> 00:54:39,380
I didn't come here just for school.

995
00:54:39,380 --> 00:54:42,780
I came here for my friends.

996
00:54:42,780 --> 00:55:08,560
It's Moe.

997
00:55:08,560 --> 00:55:34,240
But why?

998
00:55:34,240 --> 00:55:53,960
Let's go.

999
00:55:53,960 --> 00:56:10,120
Dear Kokoro Anzai, I heard from Mr. Ida that you'll be coming to school tomorrow, and he said I should write you a letter, so here it is.

1000
00:56:11,400 --> 00:56:14,160
Miss Anzai, why do you hate me?

1001
00:56:15,360 --> 00:56:18,900
All I want to do is meet with you and talk things over.

1002
00:56:18,900 --> 00:56:29,060
I guess I can understand if you're still heartbroken over Ai. However, you should know that over the summer, we broke up.

1003
00:56:30,820 --> 00:56:35,060
If you still like him, maybe I can do something to help you.

1004
00:56:40,140 --> 00:56:42,460
Come on, guys. Please be here.

1005
00:56:48,900 --> 00:56:51,960
Miss Anzai?

1006
00:57:03,300 --> 00:57:04,420
What's wrong?

1007
00:57:04,420 --> 00:57:16,820
What's a Masumune here? He's a second year.

1008
00:57:17,300 --> 00:57:17,500
Huh?

1009
00:57:18,380 --> 00:57:19,940
Maybe someone named Fuka?

1010
00:57:20,940 --> 00:57:22,260
How about Akio Subaru?

1011
00:57:23,220 --> 00:57:24,820
Those two or thirty years...

1012
00:57:24,820 --> 00:57:26,120
Calm down, Miss Anzai.

1013
00:57:26,800 --> 00:57:27,820
What's this about?

1014
00:57:28,360 --> 00:57:30,080
And there's a first year.

1015
00:57:30,400 --> 00:57:30,960
What does she know?

1016
00:57:30,960 --> 00:57:34,720
His name's not that common, so you must know him. Right?

1017
00:57:35,520 --> 00:57:38,660
I'm afraid I don't. There's no first year with that name.

1018
00:57:39,420 --> 00:57:39,720
What?

1019
00:57:40,640 --> 00:57:44,240
I might know the others, if you can tell me their last names.

1020
00:57:45,460 --> 00:57:49,660
Last names? I don't know Aki's last name. Or Fuka's.

1021
00:57:50,600 --> 00:57:51,040
Kokoro?

1022
00:57:54,180 --> 00:57:55,420
Mrs. Kirishima.

1023
00:57:55,420 --> 00:58:17,140
What are you doing here?

1024
00:58:17,800 --> 00:58:22,300
Your mother told me that you'd be here today, so I thought it would be best if I checked in on you.

1025
00:58:22,300 --> 00:58:24,560
Oh, I see.

1026
00:58:25,360 --> 00:58:26,680
Looks like you're feeling better.

1027
00:58:27,820 --> 00:58:29,560
You were so pale when I got here.

1028
00:58:31,960 --> 00:58:35,320
This is yours, right? You were clutching it in your hand.

1029
00:58:38,720 --> 00:58:41,740
I'm sorry. I read it without asking.

1030
00:58:42,000 --> 00:58:43,060
I don't want it.

1031
00:58:43,060 --> 00:58:51,020
I spoke to Mr. Iida about what happened. He was out of line.

1032
00:58:53,400 --> 00:58:56,600
I should have spoken to him about your situation from the beginning.

1033
00:58:57,620 --> 00:59:00,200
Instead, you've only been hurt more. I'm sorry.

1034
00:59:00,200 --> 00:59:07,240
I saw her. Just before, Maui told you I was there. But she ignored me, completely.

1035
00:59:08,420 --> 00:59:10,880
No, hello. No, it's good to see you.

1036
00:59:11,260 --> 00:59:13,480
She walked right by, and said nothing.

1037
00:59:14,700 --> 00:59:19,320
What if it was her? Was she the one who put Sanada's letters in my cubby?

1038
00:59:20,680 --> 00:59:22,780
Could it be that Sanada asked her to do it?

1039
00:59:22,780 --> 00:59:27,780
After all, she was the one who'd stop at my house every day to drop off school notices.

1040
00:59:29,300 --> 00:59:32,820
What if she hates me now? What do I do?

1041
00:59:33,840 --> 00:59:34,700
Don't worry.

1042
00:59:35,440 --> 00:59:36,860
We know what happened.

1043
00:59:37,460 --> 00:59:39,620
That's because somebody stepped forward and told us.

1044
00:59:39,800 --> 00:59:40,560
It was Miss Tojo.

1045
00:59:41,440 --> 00:59:41,760
Huh?

1046
00:59:42,380 --> 00:59:46,800
When she saw you, maybe she was just caught by surprise and didn't know what to say.

1047
00:59:46,800 --> 00:59:52,180
But there's one thing you can trust, and it's that your friend is clearly concerned about you.

1048
00:59:52,780 --> 00:59:55,200
Is she really? Is that true?

1049
00:59:55,540 --> 00:59:55,760
Hmm.

1050
00:59:59,680 --> 01:00:09,320
Hey, Rian.

1051
01:00:09,320 --> 01:00:17,140
The others haven't shown up yet?

1052
01:00:17,660 --> 01:00:17,940
Hmm.

1053
01:00:18,880 --> 01:00:20,260
I only just got here.

1054
01:00:20,860 --> 01:00:24,240
I had a break during soccer practice, but nobody's here.

1055
01:00:25,140 --> 01:00:26,720
Oh, so how'd it go?

1056
01:00:27,480 --> 01:00:27,940
Hmm.

1057
01:00:29,420 --> 01:00:29,940
Huh.

1058
01:00:30,620 --> 01:00:31,620
We couldn't meet up.

1059
01:00:32,280 --> 01:00:34,180
I'm not sure why, but no one came.

1060
01:00:34,500 --> 01:00:36,340
No Masamune, or the others.

1061
01:00:36,340 --> 01:00:41,660
But the really weird thing is, the nurse told me that none of them go to Yukishina.

1062
01:00:42,120 --> 01:00:42,420
Huh?

1063
01:00:43,580 --> 01:00:44,380
But how?

1064
01:00:44,640 --> 01:00:45,340
I don't know.

1065
01:00:46,600 --> 01:00:49,300
That's why I came here to ask them about it.

1066
01:00:50,420 --> 01:00:57,400
What if everything in this castle, even these mirrors, what if it's not real?

1067
01:00:57,780 --> 01:00:59,520
What if all of you don't actually exist?

1068
01:01:00,300 --> 01:01:02,820
Just thinking about that scares me.

1069
01:01:02,820 --> 01:01:02,940
What?

1070
01:01:06,340 --> 01:01:11,540
I'm real, okay?

1071
01:01:12,180 --> 01:01:13,220
I'm really here.

1072
01:01:14,120 --> 01:01:15,060
That's no lie.

1073
01:01:15,560 --> 01:01:17,580
The others, they have to be real, too.

1074
01:01:18,420 --> 01:01:19,620
Something must have kept them away.

1075
01:01:20,900 --> 01:01:25,680
This castle, along with the fact that we all met here, I think it has to mean something.

1076
01:01:26,980 --> 01:01:30,600
Also, we're all dealing with stuff that can't be random.

1077
01:01:30,600 --> 01:01:33,160
Does that mean you are, too, Rian?

1078
01:01:34,520 --> 01:01:34,960
Well.

1079
01:01:35,520 --> 01:01:39,820
So if you end up finding the key, what is it that you would want to wish for?

1080
01:01:41,940 --> 01:01:42,980
What I'd wish for?

1081
01:01:44,820 --> 01:01:45,740
It's my sister.

1082
01:01:45,980 --> 01:01:47,220
I'd wish for her to come back.

1083
01:01:47,780 --> 01:01:48,000
Huh?

1084
01:01:48,000 --> 01:01:55,680
The year I started elementary school, she got sick and died.

1085
01:01:55,880 --> 01:01:56,040
Huh?

1086
01:01:56,380 --> 01:01:57,220
My sis...

1087
01:01:57,220 --> 01:01:58,100
Sorry.

1088
01:01:58,780 --> 01:02:00,620
I know stuff like this is hard to hear.

1089
01:02:00,940 --> 01:02:01,300
Mm-mm.

1090
01:02:01,300 --> 01:02:04,880
I wasn't going to tell anyone.

1091
01:02:05,840 --> 01:02:09,140
Truth is, for a while I was set on finding the key.

1092
01:02:10,780 --> 01:02:12,680
But now I'm not so sure.

1093
01:02:15,140 --> 01:02:16,180
Compared to him?

1094
01:02:16,860 --> 01:02:18,320
My wish is so petty.

1095
01:02:18,320 --> 01:02:21,320
I should probably get back.

1096
01:02:21,700 --> 01:02:21,880
Oh.

1097
01:02:22,180 --> 01:02:23,080
I should go, too.

1098
01:02:23,480 --> 01:02:24,600
My mom is waiting for me.

1099
